## Done

- [x] Decide: macOS sandbox stays off? <!-- labels: decision -->
      Decided 2026-09-12: sandbox stays OFF on desktop, by design. Cockpit spawns shells, git, ssh, pi and LSP servers, reads any project folder and owns a Unix socket; none of that fits the App Sandbox. Sandbox is only required for the Mac App Store, which is out of scope. Hardened Runtime, notarization and TCC prompts stay. Mobile clients (iOS/Android) are sandboxed by the platform and do not run local shells. Follow-up: review whether cs.disable-library-validation is still needed in Release.entitlements.

- [x] Keyboard shortcut to switch between workspaces <!-- labels: feature -->
      Done 2026-09-12: Cmd+Shift+N (previous) and Cmd+Shift+M (next), Ctrl+Shift on Windows/Linux, in the View menu next to Select Tab. Cycles the rail in visual order (root then its worktrees), wraps around, skips the Cockpit system terminal. No digit shortcuts on purpose: worktrees make positions unstable.

- [x] Explicit approval for .env.cockpit in a freshly cloned repo <!-- labels: security -->
      Done 2026-09-12, downscoped: no trust dialog (a cloned repo already runs its own scripts and hooks). Instead: (1) keys that change who runs what are never injected (PATH, SHELL, HOME, ZDOTDIR, BASH_ENV, ENV, PROMPT_COMMAND, IFS, LD_* and DYLD_*); (2) when the .env.cockpit is tracked by git (it came with the repository) new terminals print a yellow notice listing the injected key names, never values.

- [x] Drag-and-drop a file into the terminal steals the tab focus <!-- labels: bug -->
      Fixed 2026-09-12: a native drop generates no pointer event and the drag from Finder/Explorer leaves the Cockpit window non-key, so no focus path ran. After injecting the paths the terminal now brings the window to front, focuses its pane in the VM and re-requests the terminal focus node post-frame. Needs a manual check with a real drop after the next release.

